Z||000004||Return of Fiero||11-20-2001||09:26 AM||||Personaly, as an "Audiophile" i would have never bought the 6X9's. but, if you MUST have them, there is always under the dash, but you said they were co-ax, right, hmm.. the rear wall, the side wall (both with a bit of custom finish) the door has some good room, if you dont mind cutting a bit of metal, the lower part of the dash you could put some custom boxes with some thin MDF, as the speaker is ONLY a 6X9, you dont have to worry about flex in the box, there is the custom 4X9  factory mount that could be bored out a bit, use the head reat, i think you could make it fit, but it might be too loud. i might be able to come up with more, if you want to let me think for an hour, but all of these are posibilities, from what i remeber when i did a custom instal in my 88. but i never used any of them, as they didnt have the effect i wasnted for competion.<BR>anyhow, the "spelling ace" lmao is signing off, good luck, and if you want some help in detail, write me off list at ReturnofFiero@aol.com<BR>later,<BR>Myke||||reg||1
